---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <a class="back" href="/curriculum/#lvl-B2">Back to curriculum</a>
  <p class="overline">B2 Vocabulary · Relationship, channel, purpose, and linguistic distance</p>
  <h1>Register &amp; formality</h1>
  <p class="lede">The best message is not the most formal one. It gives this reader the right facts, the right amount of distance, and a clear next action in language that fits the situation.</p>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can distinguish register, formality, tone, and politeness; identify how audience, relationship, role, purpose, channel, stakes, and shared context shape a message; choose direct or mitigated requests without confusing length with respect; use accurate request, disagreement, refusal, apology, and update patterns; shift phrasal verbs, lexical verbs, contractions, pronouns, active and passive voice, and nominalization according to their actual effect; preserve responsibility and evidence in plain professional language; recognize that professional U.S. English can be warm and contracted; hear reductions, thought groups, and contrastive prominence in polite speech; and rebuild one set of facts for an internal chat, external email, public update, and formal incident record.</p>

  <h2>Retrieve the language this lesson depends on</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered reporting force, evidence-based concession, idiom restraint, explicit agency, and audience-sensitive context before shifting register.">
    <h3>Five prerequisite decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Register prerequisite choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="asked me to send it">asked me to send it</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="however">however</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="literal wording">literal wording</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="name the responsible team">name the responsible team</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="shared context">shared context</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="use the longest words available">use the longest words available</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Priya wanted an action, not information about ability. Report <span class="ex">“Please send me the file”</span> as Priya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="asked me to send it" data-hint="Use ask plus listener plus to-infinitive for a polite action request." data-fix="Priya asked me to send it.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The proposal addresses the immediate delay. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="however" data-hint="Choose the discourse marker that concedes one strength before introducing a contrasting concern." data-fix="The proposal addresses the immediate delay; however, it does not fund the required review.">choose</button>, it does not fund the required review.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>A public safety instruction should normally prefer <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="literal wording" data-hint="Choose language that makes the required action recoverable without interpreting an idiom." data-fix="Safety instructions normally use literal wording.">choose</button> over a culture-specific metaphor.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>If the source establishes who made an operational error, a responsible update should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="name the responsible team" data-hint="Preserve supported agency instead of hiding it automatically in a passive." data-fix="Name the responsible team when that agency is established and relevant.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>A short internal chat can omit details that coworkers already know because they share <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="shared context" data-hint="Choose the background knowledge available to both writer and reader." data-fix="Shared context can make a short internal message sufficient.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice: one practical need, four appropriate messages</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Cedar Loop workshop</h3>
    <p><b>Message 1, familiar coworker in chat:</b> Can you send me the accessibility checklist by three? I need it for the venue call.</p>
    <p><b>Message 2, project partner by email:</b> Could you send me the completed accessibility checklist by 3:00 p.m.? I need it before today’s venue call. Thanks.</p>
    <p><b>Message 3, external venue coordinator:</b> Could you please confirm by 3:00 p.m. whether the north entrance will be step-free during the October 14 workshop? We need this information for the attendee notice.</p>
    <p><b>Message 4, safety instruction after confirmation:</b> Keep the north entrance clear. Do not move the temporary ramp.</p>
  </div>
  <p>The messages are not four decorative versions of one sentence. The writer changes what is explicit because each reader has different knowledge and responsibilities. The safety instruction is the most direct, but it is not the least respectful. Its purpose and consequences make directness appropriate.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You identified shared context, a polite request, explicit external reference, justified safety directness, stable core purpose, and situation-based appropriateness.">
    <h3>Discovery check: infer the situation before labeling the language</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Register discovery choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="shared project context">shared project context</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a respectful request between project partners">a respectful request between project partners</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the exact entrance, date, condition, deadline, and reason">the exact entrance, date, condition, deadline, and reason</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="ambiguity could create an access or safety problem">ambiguity could create an access or safety problem</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="obtain accurate information or protect the confirmed access arrangement">obtain accurate information or protect the confirmed access arrangement</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fits its reader, role, channel, purpose, and stakes">fits its reader, role, channel, purpose, and stakes</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="contains the rarest vocabulary">contains the rarest vocabulary</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Message 1 can say <span class="ex">the checklist</span> without naming the event because the coworkers have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="shared project context" data-hint="Choose the information already available to both participants." data-fix="The familiar coworkers share project context.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>In Message 2, <span class="ex">Could you...?</span> performs <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a respectful request between project partners" data-hint="The writer wants the partner to send a document, not report physical ability." data-fix="Could you send...? is a respectful action request here.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Because the external coordinator does not share the full project history, Message 3 states <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the exact entrance, date, condition, deadline, and reason" data-hint="Identify the references an outside reader needs to act correctly." data-fix="The external message makes the entrance, date, condition, deadline, and reason explicit.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Message 4 uses imperatives because <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="ambiguity could create an access or safety problem" data-hint="Relate the direct form to the consequence of unclear action." data-fix="A clear imperative is appropriate when ambiguity could create an access or safety problem.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Across all four messages, the practical purpose is to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="obtain accurate information or protect the confirmed access arrangement" data-hint="Preserve the operational goal even though the wording and content change." data-fix="The messages obtain accurate information or protect the confirmed access arrangement.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The strongest message is the one that <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="fits its reader, role, channel, purpose, and stakes" data-hint="Appropriateness is contextual, not a contest for the longest vocabulary." data-fix="A strong message fits its reader, role, channel, purpose, and stakes.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: register is a bundle, not a ladder</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><b>Register</b> is the recurring bundle of vocabulary, grammar, organization, reference, and spoken delivery associated with a situation or activity. <b>Formality</b> is one dimension of that bundle, often involving convention and social distance. <b>Tone</b> is the attitude or interpersonal effect a reader or listener perceives, such as warm, cautious, firm, impatient, or collaborative. <b>Politeness</b> manages relationships and expectations. These ideas interact, but they are not synonyms.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Why it matters</th><th>Possible consequence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Who is the audience?</td><td>knowledge, language needs, and expectations</td><td>define unfamiliar terms or omit shared detail</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What is our relationship?</td><td>closeness, trust, history, and social distance</td><td>choose a familiar, neutral, or more ceremonious opening</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What roles and power apply?</td><td>authority, obligation, choice, and vulnerability</td><td>avoid disguising an order as if refusal were equally available</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What action is the purpose?</td><td>request, inform, refuse, apologize, record, warn, or persuade</td><td>state the needed action and response clearly</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What is the channel or genre?</td><td>chat, call, email, notice, report, form, or legal record</td><td>adjust structure, permanence, and recoverable context</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What are the stakes?</td><td>consequences of delay, refusal, or misunderstanding</td><td>increase explicitness and reduce interpretive burden</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What context is shared?</td><td>what the reader can identify without explanation</td><td>use concise reference only when it remains unambiguous</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Do not assign one permanent register to a person</h3><p>A manager may use relaxed language in a familiar team chat and exact formal language in a compliance record. A friend may need direct literal language during an emergency. Culture, workplace practice, age, identity, and personal preference can affect expectations, but they do not let us predict every individual. Observe the actual community, explain your purpose, and repair when your first choice does not land as intended.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You diagnosed audience knowledge, relationship, role and power, purpose, channel, stakes, and shared context instead of treating formality as a single word list.">
    <h3>Diagnose seven situation variables</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Register situation variables"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="audience knowledge">audience knowledge</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="relationship">relationship</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="role and power">role and power</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="purpose">purpose</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="channel">channel</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="stakes">stakes</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="shared context">shared context</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="word length alone">word length alone</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>A public notice explains <span class="ex">north entrance</span> instead of saying <span class="ex">the usual door</span> because of the readers’ limited <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="audience knowledge" data-hint="The public may not know the team's local label." data-fix="Audience knowledge determines which references require explanation.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Two coworkers who have collaborated daily for five years may open with <span class="ex">Hi, Sam</span> because their established <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="relationship" data-hint="Choose the history and social distance between participants." data-fix="Their established relationship supports a familiar professional opening.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>A supervisor who requires attendance should say that attendance is required rather than pretending the employee has a free choice. This is a question of <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="role and power" data-hint="Identify who has authority and whether refusal is genuinely available." data-fix="Role and power affect how honestly a directive should be framed.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>An apology needs to acknowledge impact and repair, while a record needs to preserve events and times. The difference begins with communicative <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="purpose" data-hint="Ask what the message must accomplish." data-fix="Purpose distinguishes apologizing from documenting.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>An internal chat may use one short paragraph, while an incident report uses labeled fields. The relevant variable is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="channel" data-hint="Choose the medium or genre that carries the message." data-fix="Channel and genre shape organization.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>A medication warning and a lunch invitation require different degrees of explicitness because their <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="stakes" data-hint="Compare the consequences of misunderstanding." data-fix="Higher stakes usually require more explicit, testable wording.">choose</button> differ.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span><span class="ex">The revised version</span> is clear only if both participants can identify which version. That depends on <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="shared context" data-hint="Choose the information both people can recover." data-fix="Shared context makes a short reference recoverable.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose request grammar by action, choice, and consequence</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Request forms do more than move from casual to formal. They can present the action as routine, optional, burdensome, negotiable, or required. A longer indirect form is not automatically kinder. If the listener has no real choice, state the requirement and explain it instead of performing false optionality.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Typical use</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>imperative + reason</td><td>clear routine, procedure, or urgent action</td><td>Please submit the signed form by noon so payroll can process it today.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>can / could you + base verb</td><td>ordinary action request</td><td>Could you confirm the room number?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>would you mind + -ing</td><td>acknowledges some imposition</td><td>Would you mind joining ten minutes early?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>would it be possible to + base verb</td><td>asks whether an arrangement can change</td><td>Would it be possible to move the call to Friday?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>I would appreciate it if + could</td><td>more formal request with a named action</td><td>I would appreciate it if you could confirm by May 8.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>requirement + reason + support</td><td>action is obligatory, not optional</td><td>All visitors must sign in so we can account for everyone during an evacuation.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Contractions do not automatically make professional English casual</h3><p><span class="ex">I’m writing to confirm...</span>, <span class="ex">we’ve attached...</span>, and <span class="ex">I’d appreciate...</span> are common in many professional U.S. messages. An organization, legal genre, or highly ceremonial context may prefer uncontracted forms. Follow the real genre and relationship instead of applying a blanket rule.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You matched a familiar request, routine professional request, scheduling negotiation, acknowledged imposition, explicit requirement, emergency directive, formal external request, honest deadline, accessible public instruction, and professional contraction to ten contexts.">
    <h3>Complete ten request and direction choices</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Register request choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Can you send me the link when you have a minute?">Can you send me the link when you have a minute?</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Could you review the attached figures by Thursday, please?">Could you review the attached figures by Thursday, please?</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Would it be possible to move the interview to Friday morning?">Would it be possible to move the interview to Friday morning?</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Would you mind joining ten minutes early to test the captions?">Would you mind joining ten minutes early to test the captions?</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Attendance is required because this session covers the new safety procedure.">Attendance is required because this session covers the new safety procedure.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Leave through the east exit now.">Leave through the east exit now.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I would appreciate it if you could confirm receipt by May 8.">I would appreciate it if you could confirm receipt by May 8.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Please send the signed form by noon so payroll can process it today.">Please send the signed form by noon so payroll can process it today.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Select Continue, then choose the language you want.">Select Continue, then choose the language you want.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I'm writing to confirm that we've received your application.">I'm writing to confirm that we've received your application.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="A response at some vague future point might be contemplated.">A response at some vague future point might be contemplated.</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>You are messaging a familiar teammate about a nonurgent shared task: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Can you send me the link when you have a minute?" data-hint="Choose the concise familiar request with a flexible time." data-fix="Can you send me the link when you have a minute?">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>You need a colleague to check specific attached data by a real deadline: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Could you review the attached figures by Thursday, please?" data-hint="Choose the neutral-professional request that names the item and deadline." data-fix="Could you review the attached figures by Thursday, please?">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>You are asking an interviewer whether an agreed appointment can change: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Would it be possible to move the interview to Friday morning?" data-hint="Choose the pattern that treats the schedule change as negotiable." data-fix="Would it be possible to move the interview to Friday morning?">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>You recognize that an external presenter would need to give extra time for an access check: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Would you mind joining ten minutes early to test the captions?" data-hint="Choose would you mind plus -ing for an acknowledged imposition." data-fix="Would you mind joining ten minutes early to test the captions?">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>A manager is announcing a mandatory session and should not imply free choice: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Attendance is required because this session covers the new safety procedure." data-hint="State the requirement and its reason honestly." data-fix="Attendance is required because this session covers the new safety procedure.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Smoke is entering the west hallway, so a safety officer gives the immediate action: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Leave through the east exit now." data-hint="Use a short literal imperative when delay or ambiguity could cause harm." data-fix="Leave through the east exit now.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>An external reviewer needs to confirm receipt of a formal submission: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="I would appreciate it if you could confirm receipt by May 8." data-hint="Choose the formal request with a specific action and deadline." data-fix="I would appreciate it if you could confirm receipt by May 8.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Payroll genuinely needs a form today, so the writer gives an action, deadline, and reason: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Please send the signed form by noon so payroll can process it today." data-hint="A clear imperative with please and a reason can be respectful professional language." data-fix="Please send the signed form by noon so payroll can process it today.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>A public interface must tell every user exactly what to do next: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Select Continue, then choose the language you want." data-hint="Choose concise step-by-step instructions rather than social mitigation." data-fix="Select Continue, then choose the language you want.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>A normal professional U.S. email may naturally begin: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="I'm writing to confirm that we've received your application." data-hint="Choose the clear professional sentence; its contractions do not make it slang." data-fix="I'm writing to confirm that we've received your application.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Manage disagreement, refusal, and repair without hiding the message</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Diplomacy protects the working relationship while preserving the real claim. It does not require vague agreement. A useful disagreement often moves through <b>common ground + precise concern + evidence + workable alternative</b>. A useful refusal often includes <b>recognition + clear limit + brief relevant reason + possible alternative</b>. An apology needs <b>the problem + impact + responsibility + repair + next update</b> when those facts are known.</p>
  <div class="note"><h3>Respect the listener’s agency</h3><p>If you hold authority, do not make a requirement sound freely optional. If the other person can refuse, leave room for refusal. If you disagree, criticize the proposal or evidence rather than the person. If a problem affected someone, do not bury the impact beneath ceremonial language.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You built specific disagreement, clear refusal, accountable apology, proportionate urgency, genuine choice, honest authority, evidence-based challenge, and constructive redirection.">
    <h3>Choose eight relationship-sensitive moves</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Register pragmatics choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I understand the cost concern; however, the current plan does not include the required accessibility review.">I understand the cost concern; however, the current plan does not include the required accessibility review.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Thank you for inviting me. I won't be available on October 14, but I can send written comments by October 12.">Thank you for inviting me. I won't be available on October 14, but I can send written comments by October 12.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="We sent duplicate cancellation emails to 38 attendees. Their registrations remain active, and we are sending a correction now.">We sent duplicate cancellation emails to 38 attendees. Their registrations remain active, and we are sending a correction now.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Please call the emergency line now; the smell may indicate a gas leak.">Please call the emergency line now; the smell may indicate a gas leak.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="If Friday does not work, what time next week would be better?">If Friday does not work, what time next week would be better?</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="You are required to complete the access training before working at the event.">You are required to complete the access training before working at the event.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The sample includes only twelve users, so it does not yet support a general conclusion.">The sample includes only twelve users, so it does not yet support a general conclusion.</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="That option would delay the launch; could we test the smaller change first?">That option would delay the launch; could we test the smaller change first?</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Your idea is ridiculous, but whatever.">Your idea is ridiculous, but whatever.</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Disagree with a budget proposal by acknowledging the concern and identifying one specific missing requirement: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="I understand the cost concern; however, the current plan does not include the required accessibility review." data-hint="Choose common ground plus a precise evidence-based concern." data-fix="I understand the cost concern; however, the current plan does not include the required accessibility review.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Decline a workshop invitation clearly while offering a realistic alternative: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Thank you for inviting me. I won't be available on October 14, but I can send written comments by October 12." data-hint="Choose thanks, a clear limit, and a concrete alternative." data-fix="Thank you for inviting me. I won't be available on October 14, but I can send written comments by October 12.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Apologize for a confirmed communication failure without hiding the organization’s action or inventing lost registrations: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="We sent duplicate cancellation emails to 38 attendees. Their registrations remain active, and we are sending a correction now." data-hint="Name the supported problem, scope, unaffected status, and repair." data-fix="We sent duplicate cancellation emails to 38 attendees. Their registrations remain active, and we are sending a correction now.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>A possible gas leak requires proportionate urgency: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Please call the emergency line now; the smell may indicate a gas leak." data-hint="Choose immediate literal action and the reason for urgency." data-fix="Please call the emergency line now; the smell may indicate a gas leak.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>A meeting change is genuinely negotiable, so leave room for refusal: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="If Friday does not work, what time next week would be better?" data-hint="Choose the sentence that makes another option genuinely available." data-fix="If Friday does not work, what time next week would be better?">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The training is mandatory for the role, so state the requirement honestly: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="You are required to complete the access training before working at the event." data-hint="Do not disguise an employment requirement as a casual favor." data-fix="You are required to complete the access training before working at the event.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Challenge an overgeneralized research claim by identifying the evidence limit: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The sample includes only twelve users, so it does not yet support a general conclusion." data-hint="Focus on sample size and claim scope rather than the writer’s intelligence." data-fix="The sample includes only twelve users, so it does not yet support a general conclusion.">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Redirect an impractical proposal toward a testable next step: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="That option would delay the launch; could we test the smaller change first?" data-hint="Name the consequence, then propose a workable alternative." data-fix="That option would delay the launch; could we test the smaller change first?">choose</button></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use plain language at every level of formality</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Formal English does not require inflated synonyms. <span class="ex">Use</span> is usually clearer than <span class="ex">utilize</span>. <span class="ex">We reviewed the data</span> is often stronger than <span class="ex">we conducted a review of the data</span>. A phrasal verb and a single-word verb may differ in syntax, collocation, or meaning, so replace them only when the new sentence preserves the claim.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Choice</th><th>Useful effect</th><th>Risk to check</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>active subject + verb</td><td>makes responsibility and action clear</td><td>can overstate agency if the actor is uncertain</td></tr>
    <tr><td>passive voice</td><td>focuses the event, result, or unknown actor</td><td>can hide a known responsible actor</td></tr>
    <tr><td>nominalization</td><td>packages a known process as a concept</td><td>can hide who did what and increase density</td></tr>
    <tr><td>phrasal verb</td><td>may sound natural and familiar</td><td>may be ambiguous or less expected in a formal genre</td></tr>
    <tr><td>single-word lexical verb</td><td>may fit technical or formal collocation</td><td>may sound inflated or change the meaning</td></tr>
    <tr><td>explicit I / we / you</td><td>clarifies participants and responsibility</td><td>the institution may require another perspective</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Passive is a tool, not a formality switch</h3><p><span class="ex">At 9:10, 38 duplicate emails were sent</span> appropriately foregrounds the event if the actor is not yet known. Once the record establishes that the Cedar Loop scheduling team activated the wrong automation rule, <span class="ex">our scheduling team activated the wrong rule</span> preserves relevant responsibility. Choose focus from evidence and purpose, not from a rule that active is always informal or passive is always formal.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You chose plain verbs, explicit agency, justified passive focus, accurate lexical alternatives, visible action, precise scope, and reader-centered reference.">
    <h3>Complete seven clarity and responsibility decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Plain register choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="used the revised checklist">used the revised checklist</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="our scheduling team activated the wrong automation rule">our scheduling team activated the wrong automation rule</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the cause has not yet been identified">the cause has not yet been identified</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="investigate the documented complaint">investigate the documented complaint</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="reviewed the data">reviewed the data</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="affected 38 of 240 registered attendees">affected 38 of 240 registered attendees</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the application you submitted on May 3">the application you submitted on May 3</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="facilitated the utilization of said documentation">facilitated the utilization of said documentation</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The formal report remains clear when it says the team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="used the revised checklist" data-hint="Choose the common verb that preserves the exact action." data-fix="The team used the revised checklist.">choose</button>, not that it utilized the checklist.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The investigation confirms the responsible group and action, so write that <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="our scheduling team activated the wrong automation rule" data-hint="Use the established actor as subject rather than hiding it." data-fix="Our scheduling team activated the wrong automation rule.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The equipment stopped, but no source yet establishes why. The cautious incident update says <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the cause has not yet been identified" data-hint="A passive is useful when the actor or cause is genuinely unknown." data-fix="The cause has not yet been identified.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>In a formal case assignment, <span class="ex">look into</span> can be replaced without changing the purpose: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="investigate the documented complaint" data-hint="Choose the lexical verb that fits a documented inquiry, keeping its direct object." data-fix="Investigate the documented complaint.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Replace the hidden verb in <span class="ex">conducted a review of the data</span> with <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="reviewed the data" data-hint="Turn the process noun back into its direct verb." data-fix="The team reviewed the data.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The public correction should report the bounded scope: the duplicate email problem <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="affected 38 of 240 registered attendees" data-hint="Choose the exact affected group rather than implying that every registration failed." data-fix="The problem affected 38 of 240 registered attendees.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>An external follow-up is easier to identify when it refers to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the application you submitted on May 3" data-hint="Choose a reader-centered reference with the document and date." data-fix="Refer to the application you submitted on May 3.">choose</button>, not merely the aforementioned matter.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Pronunciation focus: hear respect, focus, and urgency in U.S. speech</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Politeness does not have one melody. A routine request may have a gentle fall, a rise, or a rise-fall depending on region, relationship, expectation, and conversational meaning. Speakers often group a request into a frame, action, and deadline: <span class="ex">Could you send the checklist | by THREE?</span> The most informative word in a thought group usually receives the main prominence.</p>
  <p>In fluent U.S. speech, <span class="ex">could you</span> may sound like /kʊdʒə/ and <span class="ex">would you</span> like /wʊdʒə/. <span class="ex">I would</span> often contracts to <span class="ex">I’d</span>. These reductions are options, not requirements. Preserve clearer forms when the listener, audio quality, or stakes make them useful. Contrastive prominence repairs a detail: <span class="ex">by <strong>THURSday</strong>, not <strong>FRIday</strong></span>.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read U.S. request reduction, thought-group focus, contrastive deadline, accountable apology, and safety prominence listening check" data-success-message="Correct. You heard optional could-you reduction, deadline prominence, contrastive repair, accountable impact, and action-focused safety delivery.">
    <h3>Five spoken-form decisions</h3>
    <details><summary>Tutor script and delivery notes</summary><ol><li>Could you send the checklist?</li><li>Could you CONFIRM it | by THREE?</li><li>Not THURSday | FRIday.</li><li>We sent duplicate messages to THIRty-eight attendees | and we’re sending a correction NOW.</li><li>LEAVE now | through the EAST exit.</li></ol><p>Read each line once carefully and once conversationally. Do not force the reduced forms. Keep dates, numbers, actions, and corrections recoverable, and let the communicative contrast determine the main prominence.</p></details>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Spoken register choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a natural optional reduction in fluent speech">a natural optional reduction in fluent speech</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the deadline as the newest important information">the deadline as the newest important information</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="correct Thursday to Friday">correct Thursday to Friday</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the affected group and current repair">the affected group and current repair</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the required action and safe exit">the required action and safe exit</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="equal heavy stress on every syllable">equal heavy stress on every syllable</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 1:</span> <span class="ex">Could you send the checklist?</span> Hearing <span class="ex">could you</span> as /kʊdʒə/ can be <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a natural optional reduction in fluent speech" data-hint="Treat the linked form as an option, not a rule or a sign of disrespect." data-fix="Could you may reduce naturally in fluent speech.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 2:</span> <span class="ex">Could you CONFIRM it | by THREE?</span> Main prominence on <span class="ex">three</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the deadline as the newest important information" data-hint="Identify what the listener needs to add to the shared request." data-fix="Three carries the deadline focus.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 3:</span> <span class="ex">Not THURSday | FRIday.</span> The two prominences <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="correct Thursday to Friday" data-hint="Contrastive stress rejects one day and supplies the replacement." data-fix="The speaker corrects Thursday to Friday.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 4:</span> <span class="ex">We sent duplicate messages to THIRty-eight attendees | and we’re sending a correction NOW.</span> The thought groups foreground <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the affected group and current repair" data-hint="Listen for the number in the problem and the time of the corrective action." data-fix="The speaker foregrounds the affected group and current repair.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 5:</span> <span class="ex">LEAVE now | through the EAST exit.</span> Firm prominence supports <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the required action and safe exit" data-hint="In an emergency, delivery should make action and route immediately recoverable." data-fix="The instruction foregrounds the required action and safe exit.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read the Cedar Loop record across four channels</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="reading-text">
    <p><b>Internal incident notes, October 6:</b> At 9:10 a.m., the Cedar Loop scheduling team activated the wrong automation rule. Thirty-eight of 240 registered attendees received two cancellation emails. Registration records were not deleted, and payments were not affected. Devin disabled the rule at 9:18. At 9:42, the team tested 60 fictional accounts with the corrected rule; no duplicate messages appeared. This staging test did not establish how the system would perform during the next live mailing.</p>
    <p><b>Internal chat at 9:21:</b> Devin wrote, “I turned off the rule. Registrations and payments are still intact. I’m checking the corrected version now. Can someone draft the attendee message?”</p>
    <p><b>Attendee correction sent at 10:05:</b> “This morning, we sent duplicate cancellation emails to 38 attendees. If you received two messages, please disregard the second one. Your workshop registration remains active, and no additional payment was taken. We apologize for the confusion. We corrected the mailing rule and will confirm the next workshop update by 11:00 a.m.”</p>
    <p><b>Incident record completed at 11:20:</b> “The scheduling team activated Rule C-17 instead of Rule C-12 at 9:10. The rule sent duplicate cancellation notices to 38 of 240 registered attendees. Devin Ortiz disabled C-17 at 9:18. A 60-account staging test at 9:42 produced no duplicate messages. The communications lead sent a correction at 10:05. Live-mailing reliability remains to be verified.”</p>
  </div>
